-- CONTROL for #1047: the SAME program as main.mdk with the second interface RENAMED
-- (`Speak`/`speak` in b.mdk/bi.mdk -> `Speak2`/`speak2` in b2.mdk/bi2.mdk). Nothing
-- else differs: still two unrelated modules, still two method-less impls inheriting
-- their own interface's default. It must print `A-default|B-default`. If THIS breaks,
-- cross-module default inheritance regressed generally, not #1047 specifically.
import ai.{DogA(..), sayA}
import bi2.{DogB(..), sayB}

main = println (sayA DogA ++ "|" ++ sayB DogB)
